    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.cleanroom.tooltip=Machine Type: §eCleanroom§r\nConsumes 40 EU/t when first turned on, and 4 EU/t once at 100% efficiency\nCan accept 2A from an LV energy hatch\nWill overclock and gain efficiency faster starting from HV\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§cWarning:\nBelow 100% efficiency machines inside have a chance to void outputs!\nEach maintenance issue reduces maximum efficiency by 10%\nGenerating any pollution inside causes the cleanroom to shut down\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.cleanroom.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §63-15§7x§63-15§7x§64-15§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Top center\n   §620-1007 §fPlascrete Block\n   §60-168 §fFilter Machine Casing\n   §e1 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any plascrete block\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any plascrete block\n   \nIf the width or length is even, the controller can be in either of the two middle positions\nUp to §630%§7 of the plascrete blocks can be replaced by other valid blocks:\n- Any §8EV+§7 Tiered Glass\n- Machine Hulls or Diodes for item or power transfer, respectively\n- Reinforced Doors (§oIC2§r§7). Keep closed, no gaps allowed or efficiency will drop!\n- Elevators (§oOpenBlocks§r§7) or Travel Anchors (§oEnderIO§r§7)\nSee §8config/GregTech/MachineStats.cfg§7 for more valid blocks\nUse Wireless Connectors for transferring AE2 channels\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bTotal Size\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
