    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.pcbcoolingtower.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §65§7x§65§7x§610§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §e1 §fInput Hatch: §7Bottom center casing\n   \n   §bTier 1\n   §668 §fRadiant Naquadah Alloy Casing\n   §640 §fDamascus Steel Frame Box\n   §620 §fTungstensteel Pipe Casing\n   §619 §fReinforced Photolithographic Framework Casing\n   §612 §fExtreme Engine Intake Casing\n   \n   §bTier 2\n   §648 §fInfinity Cooled Casing\n   §640 §fAmericium Frame Box\n   §639 §fReinforced Photolithographic Framework Casing\n   §620 §fTungstensteel Pipe Casing\n   §68 §fSuperconducting Coil Block\n   \nDoes not require maintenance or power\nLink to the §bPCB Factory§7 with a §aData Stick\nProjector stack size determines §bStructure Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.pcbfactory.tooltip=Machine Type: §eCircuit Board Fabricator§r\nTier of the machine determines the available recipes\nEach tier and upgrade requires additional structures\nPower consumption is multiplied by Sqrt(structures)\nTier 2 and 3 allow parallel by using extra nanites\nNanites have to be placed in a Nanite Containment Bus\nThe formula for parallels is the §6amount of nanites^0.75§7, rounded up\nMaximum parallel is §6256§7\nRecipes require a cooling upgrade to be overclocked\nLiquid Cooling uses §910 L/s§7 of §9distilled water§7 and enables default overclocks\nThermosink uses §b10 L/s§7 of §bSuper Coolant§7 and enables §dperfect overclocks\nTrace size can be changed to modify the material usage and machine speed\nConfigure Trace Size in UI\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines\nAdded by: §a§9§lBlue§b§lWeabo§r§7
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.pcbfactory.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §67§7x§67§7x§66§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §e1-2 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any lower back casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any lower back casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus: §7Any lower back casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any lower back casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any lower back casing\n   \n   §bTier 1\n   §oUnlocks T1 Recipes\n   §667-72 §fBasic Photolithographic Framework Casing\n   §640 §fDamascus Steel Frame Box\n   §625 §fPlascrete Block\n   §625 §fAny Tiered Glass\n   §612 §fGrate Machine Casing\n   §69 §fVibrant Alloy Frame Box\n   \n   §bTier 2 §9(Adds to T1)\n   §oUnlocks T2 Recipes and Parallels with Silver Nanites\n   §6158 §fReinforced Photolithographic Framework Casing\n   §634 §fDuranium Frame Box\n   §e0-1 §fNanite Containment Bus: §7Any lower back casing\n   \n   §bTier 3 §9(New Structure)\n   §oUnlocks T3 Recipes and Parallels with Gold Nanites\n   §6256-292 §fRadiation Proof Photolithographic Framework Casing\n   §676 §fRadiant Naquadah Alloy Casing\n   §e0-1 §fNanite Containment Bus: §7Any photolithographic casing\n   §e1-2 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any photolithographic casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any photolithographic casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus: §7Any photolithographic casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any photolithographic casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any photolithographic casing\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bStructure Tier\nSubchannel §bglass§7 determines §bGlass Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.plasmaforge.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePlasma Forge, DTPF§r\nTranscending Dimensional Boundaries.\nTakes §c8§7 hours of continuous run time to fully breach dimensional\nboundaries and achieve maximum efficiency, reducing fuel consumption by up to §c50%\nWhen no recipe is running, fuel discount decays x§c100§7 as fast as it builds up, draining\nthe total amount of stored runtime\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nMultidimensional spaces can be perfectly aligned and synchronized in this state, \nallowing §6Dimensional Convergence §7to occur. To reach the required stability threshold,\na §bTransdimensional Alignment Matrix §7must be placed in the controller\nWhen §6Convergence §7is active, it allows the forge to perform §cPerfect Overclocks§7,\nbut the extra power cost is instead added in form of increased catalyst amounts\nThis machine can run recipes regardless of tier, if given enough energy\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines\nAdded by: §a§4§l§o§nC§6§l§o§no§a§l§o§nl§3§l§o§ne§5§l§o§nn§r§7
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.plasmaforge.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §633§7x§633§7x§624§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Middle of the structure, 3rd layer\n   §62121 §fDimensionally Transcendent Casing\n   §62112 §fHeating Coil §b(Tiered)\n   §61250-1270 §fDimensional Injection Casing\n   §6120 §fDimensional Bridge\n   §e1-2 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any injection casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus/Hatch: §7Any injection casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus/Hatch: §7Any injection casing\n   \nSubchannel §bcoil§7 determines §bHeating Coil Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationplant.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Plant, WPP§r\nMain controller block for the Water Purification Plant\nFreely place §ePurification Units §7within §c64§7 blocks along each axis\nLeft click this controller with a data stick, then right click a purification unit to link\nSupplies power to linked purification units\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nWorks in fixed time processing cycles of §c120§7 seconds\nAll linked units follow this cycle\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nEvery recipe has a base chance of success. Success rate can be boosted\nby using a portion of the target output as a secondary input\n§c10%§7 of output yield will be consumed in exchange for an\nadditive §c15%§7 increase to success\nOn recipe failure, each purification unit has a §c50%§7 chance\nto return water of the same quality as the input or lower\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nEvery purification unit has a configuration window to configure maximum parallel amount\nThis will only scale purified water input, ALL fluid output and power usage. Other catalysts and outputs are unchanged\nToggle debug mode to reduce cycle time to 30s but disable water I/O\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oContaminants and ionized particles in water can cause significant imperfections in delicate\n§b§oprocesses related to the cutting and engraving of silicon wafers and chips. It is crucial that\n§b§othe water is systematically purified through a series of increasingly precise and complex\n§b§opurification processes, and this multiblock is the heart of the operation\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationplant.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §68§7x§67§7x§69§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 3rd layer\n   §677 §fReinforced Sterile Water Plant Casing\n   §671-72 §fSterile Water Plant Casing\n   §656 §fSuperplasticizer-Treated High Strength Concrete\n   §630 §fTungsten Frame Box\n   §66 §fTinted Industrial Glass (any color)\n   §e1-2 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Adjacent to controller\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Adjacent to controller\n   \nThe water is spawned for free once formed\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitclarifier.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Unit, CPU§r\n§b§lWater Tier: §f1§r\nMust be linked to a Purification Plant using a data stick to work\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nRequires a filter made of Activated Carbon to work\nEvery cycle, has a §c20%§7 chance to destroy the filter\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oThe first step to acquiring purified water is to filter out macroscopic contaminants through the\n§b§ouse of large physical filters. As more contaminants are captured, the efficacy of the filter\n§b§odecreases so continual replacements must be supplied to maintain full function of the Clarifier.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitclarifier.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §611§7x§611§7x§64§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 2nd layer\n   §6123-128 §fReinforced Sterile Water Plant Casing\n   §621 §fFilter Machine Casing\n   §612 §fIridium Frame Box\n   §612 §fDamascus Steel Frame Box\n   §63 §fPTFE Pipe Casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus: §7Any center side casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any center side casing\n   §e0+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any center side casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any center side casing\n   \nThe water is spawned for free once formed\nLink to the §bWater Purification Plant§7 with a §aData Stick\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitdegasifier.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Unit, DPU§r\n§b§lWater Tier: §f7§r\nMust be linked to a Purification Plant using a data stick to work\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nAt the start of the operation, the §fDegasser Control Hatch§7 will output a redstone signal\nTo succeed the recipe, you will need to successfully decode the instructions in the signal\nTo decode the signal, interpret the signal strength as a 4-bit number from 0-15\nDenote the lowest bit as bit 1, and the highest as bit 4\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§lBit 1: §9§lOzone Sparging by Inert Gas\nIf this bit is on, you must insert an §finert gas§7 into the machine\nTo determine which gas to insert, interpret bits §f2-3§7 as a 2-bit number\n§70: §c10000L §fHelium§7 / 1: §c7500L §fNeon§7 / 2: §c5000L §fKrypton§7 / 3: §c2500L §fXenon\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§lBit 2: §9§lSuperconductive Deionization\nIf this bit is on, you must insert §c1440L §fMolten Superconductor Base.\nUsing higher tier superconductor provides bonus output\nOutput multiplier: §2UV§7: §f1x§7 / §4UHV§7: §f1.25x§7 / §5UEV§7: §f1.5x§7 / §1§lUIV§7: §f1.75x§7 / §c§lUMV§7: §f2x\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§lBit 3: §9§lGravitationally-Generated Differential Vacuum Extraction\nIf this bit is on, you must insert §c4608L §fMolten Neutronium\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§lBit 4: §9§lSeldonian Settlement Process\nIf this bit is on,§c DISREGARD §7all other bits and do not insert anything\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§lNo bits: §9§lMachine Overload\nIn rare cases, the machine may overload and output no control signal at all\nTo prevent machine damage, insert §c10000L §fSuper Coolant.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nThe recipe can only succeed if the entire signal is decoded correctly\nInserting any fluid not requested by the signal will always void the recipe\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oThe penultimate stage of water purification, step seven, is an irregular series of complex\n§b§oprocesses designed to remove any residual materials left by the decontaminants from the previous\n§b§osteps such as any energetic ions, acids, clarifiers, or gasses. Depending on what the Degasser\n§b§odetects in the water, it will request various materials to complete the processes listed above.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitdegasifier.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §617§7x§617§7x§625§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 2nd layer\n   §6780-800 §fHeat-Resistant Trinium Plated Casing\n   §6622 §fOmni-Purpose Infinity Fused Glass\n   §6124 §fBedrockium Frame Box\n   §e1 §fDegasser Control Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any casing\n   \nLink to the §bWater Purification Plant§7 with a §aData Stick\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitextractor.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Unit, BPU§r\n§b§lWater Tier: §f8§r\nMust be linked to a Purification Plant using a data stick to work\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nInsert §fQuark Releasing Catalysts §7into the input bus while running\nEvery recipe cycle, a different combination of §c2§7 different §fQuark Releasing Catalysts\nwill correctly identify the lone quark and succeed the recipe\nThe order of catalysts in the combination does not matter, so §9Up§7/§dDown§7 can be identified by inserting §dDown§7/§9Up\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nEvery §c20§7 ticks, consumes ALL catalysts in the input bus\nThe base cost of inserting a catalyst is §c144L§f Molten Infinity\nFor every duplicate occurrence of an inserted catalyst in the sequence, this cost is doubled\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nKeeps track of the entire sequence of catalysts inserted this recipe\nIf the correct catalyst combination is in the sequence of inserted catalysts, immediately outputs §c2000L §fStabilised Baryonic Matter\nAt the end of a successful recipe, outputs additional §c500L §fStabilised Baryonic Matter§7 per parallel\nAt the end of the recipe, returns all incorrectly inserted catalysts in the output bus\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oThe final stage of water purification goes beyond subatomic particles and identifies the smallest\n§b§opossible imperfections within the baryons themselves. By correctly identifying which pairs of quark\n§b§oflavors are required, the unit will activate the catalysts, stabilizing the errant particles\n§b§oThis ultimately creates both Stabilised Baryonic Matter and, most importantly, absolutely perfectly purified water.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitextractor.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §617§7x§617§7x§617§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 9th layer\n   §6300-339 §fQuark Exclusion Casing\n   §6240 §fNon-Photonic Matter Exclusion Glass\n   §6108 §fBedrockium Frame Box\n   §696 §fFemtometer-Calibrated Particle Beam Casing\n   §637 §fParticle Beam Guidance Pipe Casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus: §7Any quark exclusion casing (no stocking bus)\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any quark exclusion casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any quark exclusion casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any quark exclusion casing\n   \nLink to the §bWater Purification Plant§7 with a §aData Stick\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitflocculator.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Unit, FPU§r\n§b§lWater Tier: §f3§r\nMust be linked to a Purification Plant using a data stick to work\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nSupply with §f%s§7 to operate\nOutputs §f%s§7 that can be recycled\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nDuring operation, will consume ALL §f%s§7 in the input hatch\nAt the end of the recipe, for every §c100000L §7of §f%s§7 consumed\ngain an additive §c10.0%%§7 increase to success. If total fluid supplied is not\na multiple of §c100000L§7, a penalty to success is applied using the following formula:\n§aSuccess = Success * 2^(-10 * Overflow ratio)\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oStep three in purifying water is to remove microscopic contaminants such as dusts, microplastics and other\n§b§opollutants using a clarifying agent (In this case, polyaluminium chloride) to cause flocculation - the process\n§b§oof aggregating dispersed suspended particles from a solution into larger clumps for further filtration.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitflocculator.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §68§7x§69§7x§65§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 2nd layer\n   §656-63 §fSlick Sterile Flocculation Casing\n   §630 §fSterile Water Plant Casing\n   §616 §fReinforced Sterile Water Plant Casing\n   §612 §fAdamantium Frame Box\n   §69 §fFilter Machine Casing\n   §66 §fTinted Industrial Glass (any color)\n   §e1-3 §fInput Hatch: §7Any flocculation casing\n   §e0+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any flocculation casing\n   §e1-3 §fOutput Hatch: §7Any flocculation casing\n   \nThe water is spawned for free once formed\nLink to the §bWater Purification Plant§7 with a §aData Stick\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitozonation.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Unit, OPU§r\n§b§lWater Tier: §f2§r\nMust be linked to a Purification Plant using a data stick to work\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nWill explode if the input hatch contains more than §c1024000L §fOzone Gas\nReceives a §c20%§7 bonus to success chance for every doubling of §fOzone Gas\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oThe second step in water purification is ozonation, which involves injecting large quantities of small\n§b§obubbles of highly reactive ozone gas into the water. This removes trace element contaminants like\n§b§osulfur, iron and manganese, creating insoluble oxide compounds which are then filtered out.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitozonation.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §65§7x§69§7x§610§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §696-99 §fInert Filtration Casing\n   §627 §fReactive Gas Containment Casing\n   §69 §fTinted Industrial Glass (any color)\n   §66 §fTungstensteel Frame Box\n   §63 §fPTFE Pipe Casing\n   §e2+ §fInput Hatch: §7End of reactive gas chamber (ozone), any filtration casing (water)\n   §e0+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any filtration Casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any filtration casing\n   \nLink to the §bWater Purification Plant§7 with a §aData Stick\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitphadjustment.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Unit, NPU§r\n§b§lWater Tier: §f4§r\nMust be linked to a Purification Plant using a data stick to work\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nInitial pH value every cycle varies from §c4.5§7 - §c9.5 pH\nIf the pH value is within §c0.05 pH §7of 7.0 pH at the end of the cycle, the recipe always succeeds\nOtherwise, the recipe always fails\nUse a pH Sensor Hatch to read the current pH value\nFor safety, the machine will shut down if the pH goes below 0 or exceeds 14\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nEvery §c20§7 ticks, consumes ALL §f%s§7 and §f%s§7 in the special hatches\n§cRaises §7the pH value by §c0.01 pH §7per piece of §fSodium Hydroxide Dust\n§cLowers §7the pH value by §c0.01 pH §7per §c10L §7of §fHydrochloric Acid\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oThe fourth step of water purification is to neutralize the solution and bring its pH to exactly 7, rendering\n§b§othe solution inert with no hydrogen ion activity beyond water’s natural amphiproticity. Acids and bases from soils\n§b§oand geology cause natural alkalinity variations in water which can cause corrosive reactions with sensitive\n§b§omaterials. This necessitates the use of the corresponding neutralizing agents to pH balance the water.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitphadjustment.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §65§7x§615§7x§66§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 2nd layer\n   §6134 §fInert Neutralization Water Plant Casing\n   §648 §fNaquadah Alloy Frame Box\n   §618 §fChemical Grade Glass\n   §612-17 §fStabilized Naquadah Water Plant Casing\n   §e0-2 §fpH Sensor Hatch: §7Below controller\n   §e1 §fInput Bus: §7Top of left chamber (sodium hydroxide)\n   §e2+ §fInput Hatch: §7Top of right chamber (hydrochloric acid), behind controller (water)\n   §e1+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Behind controller\n   \nLink to the §bWater Purification Plant§7 with a §aData Stick\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitplasmaheater.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Unit, TPU§r\n§b§lWater Tier: §f5§r\nMust be linked to a Purification Plant using a data stick to work\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nComplete heating cycles by first heating the water to §c10000K§7,\nand then cooling it back down to §c0K\nInitial temperature is reset to §c0K§7 on recipe start\nEach completed heating cycle boosts success chance by §c33%\nIf the temperature ever reaches §c12500K§7 the recipe will fail and output steam\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nConsumes up to §c10L/s §fHelium Plasma§7 and up to §c100L/s §fSuper Coolant\n§cRaises §7the temperature by §c100K§7 per liter of plasma consumed\n§cLowers §7the temperature by §c5K§7 per liter of coolant consumed\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oStep five of water purification is to evaporate complex organic polymers and extremophile organisms\n§b§othat might be resistant to simple acids, clarifying agents, and filters. Using an ultra high\n§b§opressure chamber in combination with extreme temperature fluctuations allows the water to remain\n§b§osupercritical while evaporating any remaining contaminants, ready for filtration\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunitplasmaheater.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §615§7x§623§7x§615§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §6672 §fReinforced Sterile Water Plant Casing\n   §664 §fTinted Industrial Glass (any color)\n   §650-53 §fHeat-Resistant Trinium Plated Casing\n   §640 §fSuperconductor Base ZPM Frame Box\n   §69 §fSuperconducting Coil Block\n   §68 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e3+ §fInput Hatch: §7Bottom left of chamber (plasma), front bottom center of tower (coolant), any trinium casing (water)\n   §e1+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any trinium casing\n   \nLink to the §bWater Purification Plant§7 with a §aData Stick\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.purificationunituvtreatment.tooltip=Machine Type: §ePurification Unit, LPU§r\n§b§lWater Tier: §f6§r\nMust be linked to a Purification Plant using a data stick to work\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nDuring operation, swap the lens in the §fLens Housing\nThe multiblock will output a signal through the §fLens Indicator Hatch\nwhen the current lens must be swapped\nLens swaps will be requested in random intervals of §c3 to 15s\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nSuccess chance is boosted by §c10.0% §7for each successful swap performed.\nRemoving a lens too early will fail the recipe\nFind the order of lenses in the recipe in NEI,\nor use a portable scanner to view the currently requested lens\nThe recipe always starts at the Orundum Lens\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§b§oThe sixth step of water purification involves identifying any remaining negatively charged ions within\n§b§othe water which may cause electrical faults in future wafer manufacturing. Bombarding the water with varying\n§b§owavelengths of photon beams will impart energy into outer-shell electrons, causing them to detach from the\n§b§oatoms themselves and pass through the walls of the tank, ensuring the water is perfectly electrically polar.\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
