    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.wormhole.tooltip=Machine Type: §eWormhole Generator, MWG§r\nTransfers EU between two wormhole generators\nWormholes are linked by placing an AE2 Entangled Singularity in each controller slot\nThe transfer rate is limited by the wormhole size, and the wormhole size is governed by the transfer rate\nIf the transfer rate is completely stable, the transfer efficiency is 99.5%\nEU will only be transferred if there is space in the laser source hatch\nEach laser target must have a laser source on the §oother§7 controller, on the §oopposite§7 side\nConsumes an AE2 Singularity from an input bus each time the wormhole is kick-started\nRight click the controller with a screwdriver to disable overclocking\nEnergy Hatch limited by §fGlass§7 Tier\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines\nAdded by: §a§9Recursive Pineapple§7, Rendering by: §fBucketBrigade§r§7
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.wormhole.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §67§7x§67§7x§67§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 4th layer\n   §60-51 §fHigh Power Casing\n   §636 §fAny Tiered Glass §b(Tiered)\n   §624 §fMolecular Casing\n   §622 §fFusion Coil Block\n   §68 §fEuropium Reinforced Radiation Proof Machine Casing\n   §e0-4 §fLaser Target Hatch: §7Any center side casing\n   §e0-4 §fLaser Source Hatch: §7Any center side casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any high power casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus: §7Any high power casing\n   \nInsert an entangled singularity into the controller to link it with another one\nEach laser target hatch must have a corresponding laser source hatch\non the other linked generator on the opposite side\nSubchannel §bglass§7 determines §bGlass Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine_dronecentre.tooltip=Machine Type: §eDrone Centre§r\n§4DEPRECATED - Controller will be removed in next major update!\n§4Check NEI for new Controller and conversion recipe\n§bDrone #10032, cleared for takeoff!\nMonitors multiblock machines in range\nReplace maintenance hatch on other multi with drone downlink module\nProvides maintenance, power control, monitoring, and more\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nOperation range is determined by drone tier:\nT1-128, T2-512, T3-4096, T4-4096(Auto)/Infinite(Key)\nT4 drone allows cross-dimension connection!\n§cTo enable cross-dimension,\n§cdownlink module must have the same key with centre.\n§cBut it's not necessary for auto connection in range\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nPlace drones in input bus; only one needed to operate\nAutomatically upgrade based on the drone level in the input bus\nThere is a chance per second that the drone will crash\nChance is determined by drone tier: T1: 1/28800, T2: 1/172800, T3 & T4: 0\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines\nAdded by: §a§bSilverMoon§r§7\nStructure by: §a§6omegacubed§r§7
