    S:gt.blockmachines.solartower.controller.tier.single.tooltip=Machine Type: §eSolar Tower§r\nContributing Green Energy towards the future\nSurround with rings of Solar Reflectors\nThe Reflectors increase the internal heat value of the Tower (see below for formula)\nEach Reflector ring increases tier, the first ring is required for the Tower to work\nInput: Solar Salt (Cold)\nOutput: Solar Salt (Hot)\nEvery cycle (10 seconds), heat increases and all the Cold Solar Salt is heated\nConverting Cold to Hot Solar Salt reduces heat, equal to the amount converted\nThis conversion only happens if heat >= 30000 and controller efficiency = 100%\nIf there's more Cold Salt than heat, all the heat is used up and returns to 0\nThe heat increase is most efficient at exactly half of maximum heat\nMinimum efficiency at 0 or 100000 heat, maximum efficiency at 50000\nHeat Efficiency formula: ( 7000 - [|currentHeat - 50000| ^ 0.8]) / 7000\nHeat gain per cycle: numberHeaters * heatEfficiency * (10 + bonus)\nBonus: 1 ring  = +1, 2 rings = +2, 3 rings = +4, 4 rings = +8, 5 rings = +16\nTotal number of reflectors based on how many rings are built:\n1 ring = 36, 2 rings = 88, 3 rings = 156, 4 rings = 240, 5 rings = 340\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.solartower.controller.tier.single.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §615-31§7x§615-31§7x§628§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Top center, 28th layer\n   §636/88/156/240/340 §fSolar Reflector\n   §6229-250 §fStructural Solar Casing\n   §666 §fSalt Containment Casing\n   §660 §fThermal Containment Casing\n   §660 §fThermally Insulated Casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any bottom side casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any bottom side casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any bottom side casing\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bNumber of Rings\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.sparge.controller.single.tooltip=Machine Type: §eGas Sparge Tower§r\nRuns gases through depleted molten salts to extract precious fluids\nWorks the same way as the Distillation Tower, but with a fixed height of 8\nFluids are outputted one per layer based on the slot number in NEI\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.sparge.controller.single.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §63§7x§63§7x§68§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §645-56 §fSparge Tower Exterior Casing\n   §e1+ §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any bottom casing\n   §e7 §fOutput Hatch: §7One per layer, except the bottom layer\n   §fMandatory Air: §7Interior of the structure\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.substation.01.input.single.tooltip=Machine Type: §eEnergy Buffer, PSS§r\nConsumes 5% of the average voltage of all energy type hatches\nDoes not require maintenance\nCan be built with variable height between 4-18\nHatches can be placed nearly anywhere\nHV Energy/Dynamo Hatches are the lowest tier you can use\nSupports voltages >= UHV using MAX tier components\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
